# Vibely (internal) — dev-server plumbing & build caches
#
# A PREFIX, not an enumeration. This list used to name the dotfiles one by one
# and had already fallen behind twice: `.vibely-inspector-tagger.js` and
# `.vibely-hmr-gate.js` are written into the workspace on every dev-server
# launch and matched none of them, so they showed up as untracked files in the
# user's own repository. The same rule is spelled `isVibelyInfraFile`
# (sandbox/path-utils.ts) for the editor tree and git sync, and `**/.vibely-*`
# in the watcher's ignore list — all three have to agree, and a glob is the only
# form of this rule that cannot go stale.
nohup.out
*.tsbuildinfo
.vibely-*

